# Normalize line endings in the repository, independent of each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Without this file, a contributor whose core.autocrlf is false on Windows
# commits CRLF, and the Linux checkout (the PythonAnywhere deployment, D-08)
# receives CRLF. Verified in a scratch repository on git 2.55.0: the same file
# is stored as i/crlf without this rule and i/lf with it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide per file, so files it detects as binary are left
# byte-for-byte alone. That is what keeps the DEL-04 evidence screenshots intact.
* text=auto
